---

# Welcome

This presentation demonstrates the new abstract code highlighting features.

===

## Line-by-Line Highlighting

Shows each line progressively:

```javascript [highlight:line-by-line]
function greet(name) {
    console.log('Hello ' + name);
    return true;
}
```

===

## Block Highlighting

Highlights blocks separated by empty lines:

```javascript [highlight:block]
function first() {
    console.log('First function');
}

function second() {
    console.log('Second function');
}

function third() {
    console.log('Third function');
}
```

===

## Function Highlighting

Detects and highlights functions individually:

```javascript [highlight:function]
function add(a, b) {
    return a + b;
}

function multiply(a, b) {
    return a * b;
}

function divide(a, b) {
    if (b === 0) return null;
    return a / b;
}
```

===

## Class Highlighting

Highlights class definitions:

```javascript [highlight:class]
class Animal {
    constructor(name) {
        this.name = name;
    }
    
    speak() {
        console.log(this.name + ' makes a sound');
    }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    speak() {
        console.log(this.name + ' barks');
    }
}
```

===

## All at Once

Highlights everything immediately:

```javascript [highlight:all]
const x = 10;
const y = 20;
const sum = x + y;
console.log(sum);
```

===

## No Highlighting

No progressive highlighting:

```javascript [highlight:none]
const x = 10;
const y = 20;
const sum = x + y;
console.log(sum);
```

===

## Reveal.js Compatible

Still supports traditional reveal.js syntax:

```javascript [lines:'1,3|2,4']
const x = 10;
const y = 20;
const sum = x + y;
console.log(sum);
```

===

## Mixed Syntax

Can combine highlight mode with start offset:

```python [highlight:function start:10]
def calculate(x, y):
    result = x + y
    return result

def process(data):
    cleaned = data.strip()
    return cleaned.upper()
```

===

## Thank You!

Try the new highlighting modes in your presentations!
